=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play logs/empty ----------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Logs screen proposed for slice 1,$
# inferred from v0.3.2 and origin/main, read from a simulated$
# host by the gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s to build. It only$
# reads: no plan, no y/N, no journal. No pager runs: an item$
# says what it would run. Nothing on this machine changes: every$
# command and file is the fake's.$
$
# Info: logs/empty$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13, less installed. The file is$
# there and empty. Nearly unreachable today, as start-up has$
# written to it by the time the screen can read it$
# (cmd/hardn/main.go:57, :155, :185; config.go:246;$
# osdetect.go:93-95): only if hardn's own open failed, the file$
# was truncated while hardn runs, or under next/p3-startup.$
$
# Logs #########################################################$
$
# File ---------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Path                 /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  Empty$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Refresh              Read the log again$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

